- Story & Context: Hongdae busking folklore now insists the capsule was never buried by civil engineers, but abandoned in 1994 by four conservatory deserters who swore to dissolve their songs into the estuarine silt rather than submit to the national registry. Scavengers still walk the reeds near the Imjin River at daybreak, dragging neodymium magnets through the gray clay to recover fragments of the ferric ribbon that allegedly stained the tide pools the color of bruised plums. Over an ascendant, cloud-like swell of overblown wooden piccolos and disintegrated guitar picking, the track slowly evaporates into raw tape hiss: "The territory is gone, but the wind remembers the gate."
